        "results_interpretation": "This meta-analysis, incorporating data from six studies, found a pooled effect size of 1.18 (95% CI: 0.92 to 1.52) for the association between carnitine intake and breast cancer incidence. The confidence interval includes 1, and the statistical analysis concludes that carnitine exposure is not associated with breast cancer risk. Notably, the heterogeneity among studies was substantial (I\u00b2 = 92.25%), suggesting considerable variation in reported results, which may limit the reliability of the pooled estimate. This high degree of heterogeneity indicates that further investigation is warranted to explore potential sources of variability between included studies."
